WEBVTT

00:06.960 --> 00:10.230
This is for taking care of the kid,
and your wedding present.

00:10.680 --> 00:12.400
I'd be honored if you'd accept.

00:16.000 --> 00:16.990
Oh, wow!

00:17.270 --> 00:19.740
Couples' tickets to that theme park in Maihama!

00:20.060 --> 00:24.000
Yes, sir. I figured young lovers
oughta have a good time, y'know?

00:24.000 --> 00:26.960
This is great! Thanks, Ginga-kun!

00:26.960 --> 00:29.500
You two enjoy yourselves.

00:31.250 --> 00:34.800
Tsukasa-chan, is this your first
time going to the Dream Kingdom?

00:34.800 --> 00:37.970
Do you think I'd be this
excited if it wasn't?

00:37.970 --> 00:39.010
Good point.

00:39.010 --> 00:42.750
They even say there's a superstition
about a spell being cast on you...

00:42.750 --> 00:44.020
Sounds about right.

00:44.560 --> 00:47.080
Now that you mention it,
have you been there before?

00:47.080 --> 00:49.390
Yep. Twice, when I was little.

00:49.390 --> 00:50.460
I see.

00:50.980 --> 00:51.650
In that case...

00:52.230 --> 00:54.150
You must know all the tips and tricks!

00:55.550 --> 00:58.660
Let's get to bed early so
we'll be ready for tomorrow.

00:59.110 --> 01:01.700
We're not gonna win tomorrow
without a strategy gui—

01:02.670 --> 01:04.660
That was fast! She's already out!

01:05.060 --> 01:07.580
She's really looking forward to it, huh?

01:07.930 --> 01:11.710
I'm actually getting nervous about
how high her anticipation is.

01:12.080 --> 01:13.750
I'm counting on you, Dream Kingdom!

01:13.750 --> 01:17.230
You somehow have to surpass my
wife's overflowing hype levels!

02:53.070 --> 02:55.520
But the skies were clear
when we left the house...

02:56.000 --> 02:59.130
I-I guess it started raining, Tsukasa-chan.

02:59.760 --> 03:00.810
Sure did!

03:00.810 --> 03:04.280
Since we don't have time to buy
umbrellas, let's rush to the entrance!

03:05.160 --> 03:08.360
Come on! It's almost opening time!
We better get going!

03:10.100 --> 03:13.730
Okay, folks, have a good time!

03:15.420 --> 03:16.960
Wow!

03:17.340 --> 03:19.720
So this is what it's like...

03:19.720 --> 03:22.220
There's cute stuff every way you turn!

03:22.220 --> 03:24.470
How do you even know where to start?

03:24.900 --> 03:28.790
Let's start with getting passes
for the most popular attractions,

03:28.790 --> 03:31.280
and then see what we'll be able
to ride in the meantime.

03:31.280 --> 03:34.200
Those are the priority passes, right?

03:34.200 --> 03:36.130
We'll definitely need those!

03:36.130 --> 03:37.150
Let's get to it!

03:37.150 --> 03:38.290
But first...

03:43.660 --> 03:45.920
Of course! Raincoats!

03:45.920 --> 03:47.740
These are gonna come in handy!

03:48.020 --> 03:50.500
I only bought them so we'd keep dry, but...

03:50.990 --> 03:53.750
My wife is super cute in a raincoat!

03:57.680 --> 04:00.240
I guess rain can be nice sometimes!

04:01.220 --> 04:03.010
I keep asking, but...

04:03.370 --> 04:06.460
Why did we have to come here in the rain?

04:06.460 --> 04:10.890
Now, now. I'm pretty sure we're gonna
get a glimpse of something fun.

04:14.700 --> 04:16.520
Oh, hell no!

04:16.910 --> 04:20.400
What are those two doing having a date at
an amusement park, being all lovey-dovey?!

04:20.400 --> 04:22.210
I mean, they're married.

04:22.210 --> 04:25.410
A lovey-dovey date at an amusement
park seems par for the course.

04:26.160 --> 04:28.240
Which is why, today...

04:28.240 --> 04:32.640
We're here to see how those two
flirt here, at an amusement park,

04:32.640 --> 04:34.400
for the historical record!

04:34.400 --> 04:36.790
How is that historically significant?!

04:36.790 --> 04:38.290
But first...

04:38.650 --> 04:42.350
I got our passes, so let's head to
Big Thunder Fujiyama right now!

04:42.350 --> 04:44.210
Well-played, Charlotte!

04:44.210 --> 04:46.040
I thought we were following them?

04:46.040 --> 04:48.300
Yeah, but don't you wanna
hit the rides first?

04:56.690 --> 04:58.800
I wanna check that out!

04:58.800 --> 04:59.440
What?

05:00.130 --> 05:02.190
Oh, Kerenagure Mansion.

05:02.850 --> 05:04.420
Okay, let's check it out.

05:11.550 --> 05:13.590
The atmosphere in here is really something.

05:13.590 --> 05:15.150
Sure is.

05:17.060 --> 05:19.460
Look, darling! Get a load of that thing!

05:19.730 --> 05:21.210
It's pretty impressive.

05:21.710 --> 05:25.630
I see. This kind of detailed production

05:25.630 --> 05:28.220
must be pretty striking
when it's your first time.

05:28.640 --> 05:30.720
Looks like we get in these!

05:31.040 --> 05:35.090
Still, this attraction's
been around for a long time.

05:35.980 --> 05:38.980
I'm not sure if it'll really
impress Tsukasa-chan.

05:39.680 --> 05:43.980
I'm counting on you, Dream Kingdom!
Show off your potential!

05:49.710 --> 05:50.740
Look at that!

05:51.630 --> 05:53.740
Seems like a good reaction!

05:54.240 --> 05:56.250
How'd you like your first
visit to that attraction?

05:58.350 --> 06:01.130
Looks like you enjoyed it. I'm glad.

06:01.130 --> 06:03.280
This place really is amazing!

06:03.280 --> 06:05.870
We've got to make sure
to clear the entire park!

06:05.870 --> 06:07.510
Okay, then, next is...

06:08.000 --> 06:10.760
This one! Space Sagittarius Tours!

06:10.760 --> 06:13.760
Oh, the one based on the
popular movie series?

06:17.160 --> 06:22.140
Wow, they did a good job of
reproducing the look of the films.

06:22.140 --> 06:23.760
You can tell?

06:23.760 --> 06:26.400
There's the android from Episode III.

06:26.740 --> 06:29.910
That's the space ship from Episode V.

06:30.310 --> 06:33.280
You really know a lot about this stuff, huh?

06:34.020 --> 06:35.810
It's common knowledge, dear.

06:44.420 --> 06:46.420
This really is cool!

06:46.920 --> 06:48.420
Keep it up, Dream Kingdom!

06:48.900 --> 06:51.430
I bet Tsukasa-chan is loving this!

06:54.140 --> 06:56.490
That was really amazing, huh, Tsukasa-chan?

06:57.370 --> 06:59.570
Huh? What's wrong?

06:59.570 --> 07:00.440
Darling...

07:01.080 --> 07:03.190
I wanna go on that one again.

07:04.310 --> 07:08.190
But if we do, it'll eat into our
time for riding other stuff...

07:10.340 --> 07:12.540
The crowd's light today because of the rain.

07:12.540 --> 07:14.200
You'll get a chance again later.

07:16.200 --> 07:19.020
Yanagi-sensei! What brings you here?

07:19.020 --> 07:21.960
Oh, come on. Everyone goes to theme parks.

07:22.530 --> 07:27.010
I took a cue from you two and
decided I could use a break.

07:27.010 --> 07:30.510
I see! So, are you here with your boyfriend?

07:31.970 --> 07:33.730
Well... no...

07:33.730 --> 07:36.720
I'm actually with here with
another teacher from work.

07:37.090 --> 07:40.160
I've never gone to one of
these places with a boyfriend.

07:40.160 --> 07:43.430
In fact, I've never had a boyfriend.

07:43.430 --> 07:45.480
I'm really sorry.

07:45.480 --> 07:49.730
Oh, but the coworker who
came with me is a man!

07:49.730 --> 07:52.510
So maybe, from a distance,
we look like we're together?

07:52.510 --> 07:55.990
I-I bet you do! You're bound
to look like a couple!

07:55.990 --> 07:58.920
Where is the other teacher
you came with, though?

07:58.920 --> 08:03.500
I think he's getting a pass for one
of the more popular attractions.

08:04.000 --> 08:08.540
This is actually my first time here,
and I don't really get how it works.

08:09.630 --> 08:14.260
He said he won the tickets
to the park, too, I think.

08:16.080 --> 08:18.060
Would you really invite a coworker

08:18.060 --> 08:21.590
you're not interested in with tickets
you just happened to win?

08:21.590 --> 08:23.270
No! The answer is no, I say!

08:23.780 --> 08:26.440
The idea that he was able to stumble
into tickets so conveniently

08:26.440 --> 08:28.160
is already out of the question!

08:28.160 --> 08:31.280
But considering how nice this place is,

08:31.620 --> 08:34.780
I bet it'd be wonderful
to come here on a date.

08:35.150 --> 08:39.260
Is that a possibility with
this coworker of yours?

08:40.080 --> 08:44.210
Oh, no way! I'm so boring,

08:44.210 --> 08:46.180
there's no way he'd be interested!

08:47.000 --> 08:50.890
His name is Taniguchi-sensei,

08:50.890 --> 08:53.760
and he's pretty sweet,
always inviting me to movies and such,

08:53.760 --> 08:56.480
because he knows I don't get out much.

08:56.480 --> 09:00.060
A rom-com! This situation is
directly out of a rom-com!

09:00.830 --> 09:04.700
Taniguchi-sensei is the protagonist,
and Yanagi-sensei the love interest!

09:04.700 --> 09:08.330
It's a romantic comedy about
the efforts of Taniguchi-sensei

09:08.330 --> 09:11.070
to romance the super-oblivious Yanagi-sensei!

09:11.360 --> 09:14.140
Which means we need to get out of here fast!

09:14.140 --> 09:18.620
If Taniguchi-sensei comes back,
the date he arranged at a theme park

09:18.620 --> 09:22.330
could end up falling apart due to
the appearance of acquaintances!

09:22.620 --> 09:26.130
It's clear to me what needs to be done.

09:26.130 --> 09:30.340
Evacuate! We clear out at full speed,
with no regard for manners or shame!

09:30.690 --> 09:34.720
Oh, darling! Isn't it time for
that ride we got a pass for?

09:34.720 --> 09:36.340
Huh? No, not ye—

09:36.340 --> 09:39.790
But we better line up right away,
before the seats are all full!

09:39.790 --> 09:41.350
Gotta hurry!

09:41.350 --> 09:44.090
Well, Sensei, we'll see you around!

09:44.090 --> 09:47.350
Okay! Let's all have a good time!

09:48.950 --> 09:51.110
That was a really close one, darling.

09:51.660 --> 09:55.860
We almost ended up torpedoing
Taniguchi-sensei's plan.

09:56.300 --> 09:57.910
Wait, what do you mean?

09:58.910 --> 10:02.750
I mean that he probably
didn't win those tickets!

10:03.520 --> 10:05.210
Wh-Wh-Wh-What makes you say that?

10:05.210 --> 10:08.500
He had to act like he did in
order to invite Yanagi-sensei.

10:09.550 --> 10:13.750
As smart as you are, darling, you're really
clueless about this sort of thing.

10:15.730 --> 10:20.000
There's only one reason a guy would
ask a girl to an amusement park.

10:20.000 --> 10:23.890
I'm saying Taniguchi-sensei
likes Yanagi-sensei.

10:26.370 --> 10:27.680
Really?!

10:27.680 --> 10:31.400
That's right! And having acquaintances around
would put a damper on a romantic mood, right?

10:31.620 --> 10:33.400
Oh, yeah...

10:33.400 --> 10:36.280
But from the way Yanagi-sensei
was talking about it,

10:36.640 --> 10:38.870
I don't think she has any clue at all.

10:39.810 --> 10:42.660
I don't think she does.
Which is why I'm betting...

10:43.410 --> 10:46.250
Taniguchi-sensei is playing for keeps.

10:46.250 --> 10:49.410
It's a do-or-die challenge,
like entering the World Cup.

10:50.960 --> 10:52.830
But putting that aside,

10:52.830 --> 10:55.690
we should head to our next attraction.

10:55.690 --> 10:56.460
Sure.

10:59.200 --> 11:00.390
This one is next!

11:00.390 --> 11:02.270
How do I even describe this?

11:02.270 --> 11:03.980
They really went for it with this one!

11:03.980 --> 11:06.410
Yeah. They're definitely not being shy.

11:07.750 --> 11:10.690
Hey, Tsukasa-chan, there's Yanagi-sensei.

11:11.120 --> 11:14.980
Looking at them like this, I bet
anyone could tell he's interested.

11:14.980 --> 11:17.190
It's basically written all over his face.

11:17.760 --> 11:19.790
He made the right move inviting her,

11:19.790 --> 11:22.080
but unless he earns enough
points with this outing,

11:22.080 --> 11:24.320
she's just gonna think he's a "nice guy."

11:26.360 --> 11:27.650
Now, what's his play?

11:27.650 --> 11:29.200
How will Taniguchi make his approach?

11:33.230 --> 11:34.790
And he reaches out!

11:34.790 --> 11:36.840
Can Taniguchi pull this off?!

11:41.350 --> 11:42.630
No goal!

11:42.630 --> 11:45.600
He's really feeling that
indecision right now!

11:47.090 --> 11:51.180
Th-This is a pretty tense conflict.

11:51.180 --> 11:53.600
It's really frustrating, actually!

11:53.600 --> 11:59.040
There's no way he'll be able to earn points
from Yanagi-sensei if he's being so timid!

11:59.040 --> 12:00.110
You're right about that.

12:00.580 --> 12:03.110
He might have a fatal mental weakness.

12:04.390 --> 12:08.240
And Yanagi-sensei does seem kind
of dense about this sort of thing.

12:08.240 --> 12:11.200
I guess she's the same type as you, darling.

12:11.570 --> 12:15.080
Aw, come on! I think I'm pretty perceptive.

12:17.310 --> 12:21.090
Still, with how dense she is, it might
end up having the reverse effect.

12:22.320 --> 12:26.090
This attraction is a dark,
slightly scarier one...

12:26.090 --> 12:29.020
Th-This is pretty exciting, huh?

12:29.020 --> 12:30.920
Y-Yeah, I think so.

12:31.530 --> 12:33.830
Um, Taniguchi-sensei...

12:33.830 --> 12:37.110
I, um... scare pretty easily, so...

12:39.380 --> 12:43.110
Is it okay if we hold hands
until the ride's over?

12:45.350 --> 12:46.980
Goal!

12:46.980 --> 12:49.990
Taniguchi ends up giving up a goal instead!

12:54.000 --> 12:57.330
That really was one heck of a goal.

12:57.330 --> 12:59.540
She landed it clean, too.

13:00.000 --> 13:02.480
You think he has any chance
of turning this around?

13:02.480 --> 13:04.470
I'm not really sure.

13:05.020 --> 13:10.880
But there's still eating out, seeing the
lights, the parade, and the fireworks show.

13:10.880 --> 13:12.970
So he'll have more chances to rack up points!

13:13.280 --> 13:16.570
Wait, there's all that stuff, too?
That sounds awesome!

13:28.820 --> 13:31.830
Taniguchi-sensei really
isn't getting anywhere.

13:32.110 --> 13:35.170
If he likes her, he should just tell her.

13:35.170 --> 13:39.580
I'm sure even teachers don't have
the answers when it comes to love.

13:42.820 --> 13:46.160
Should I tell her now? Or is it too early?

13:46.160 --> 13:49.790
Do I need a more romantic atmosphere first?!

13:49.790 --> 13:51.720
Somebody, please, tell me!

13:52.320 --> 13:55.600
Why did you invite me today, anyway?

13:56.450 --> 13:58.850
Uh, well, er, I...

13:59.110 --> 14:03.360
This is bad! I didn't think she'd
give me an opening like this!

14:03.780 --> 14:06.050
Wait, but maybe it's my chance!

14:06.050 --> 14:11.120
I can use a good old-fashioned,
"Well, obviously because I like you, Sensei!"

14:11.120 --> 14:12.120
Okay!

14:12.500 --> 14:14.190
W-Well, it's because...

14:14.190 --> 14:16.780
Hey, why did you invite me today?

14:16.780 --> 14:19.370
W-Well... the reason is...

14:19.820 --> 14:22.130
Because I like you, obviously!

14:22.380 --> 14:25.130
What are you doing, kid?! In front
of all these people?! Seriously?!

14:25.130 --> 14:27.590
Oh, I'm so glad! Then you want to go out?

14:27.590 --> 14:28.630
Yeah, of course!

14:28.630 --> 14:30.130
You stupid, crazy idiot!

14:30.130 --> 14:33.260
Don't you realize there are tons of
people in your situation in this park?!

14:35.400 --> 14:37.770
And Yanagi-sensei is paying close attention!

14:37.770 --> 14:41.900
Wait, so that stuff about winning
the tickets wasn't true, was it?

14:41.900 --> 14:44.340
Please! Please stop, I'm begging you!

14:44.340 --> 14:46.650
You're ruining my plan!

14:46.920 --> 14:48.380
Well, yeah, of course!

14:48.380 --> 14:51.030
I said that because I wanted
to invite you on a date.

14:51.030 --> 14:53.590
And I am done.

14:54.420 --> 14:56.470
Did you hear all that, Taniguchi-sensei?

14:56.470 --> 14:57.660
Y-Yeah.

14:58.350 --> 15:03.040
I guess not many people actually
win tickets like you did, huh?

15:05.180 --> 15:06.550
Thank... goodness?

15:06.550 --> 15:09.050
I guess she didn't catch on!

15:09.550 --> 15:12.170
Wait, if she didn't figure
it out after all that...

15:12.170 --> 15:15.060
It means she has absolutely no
romantic interest in me, right?

15:15.320 --> 15:18.560
That seems like despairingly bad odds.

15:18.860 --> 15:22.070
How do I even broach the
subject of romance now?

15:23.760 --> 15:25.570
Oh, look, Taniguchi-sensei.

15:25.920 --> 15:29.570
What's that crowd in
front of the clock tower?

15:31.820 --> 15:34.320
Oh, I think it's a wedding.

15:34.320 --> 15:36.100
A w-wedding?

15:36.100 --> 15:39.150
People get married at theme parks?

15:39.150 --> 15:43.000
They do. It costs a whole
lot of money, though.

15:43.830 --> 15:48.920
But it's pouring today...
And her dress is soaked.

15:48.920 --> 15:52.340
Yeah, but it's not like they can call it off.

15:53.240 --> 15:55.630
I bet they were hoping for better weather.

15:55.630 --> 15:58.260
They're starting their new life together.

15:58.260 --> 16:01.100
Still, he's doing better than I am right now.

16:02.380 --> 16:04.390
They look happy.

16:05.670 --> 16:07.470
I mean, look at them.

16:07.910 --> 16:12.280
They just got married, and they've
already been put through a test like this,

16:12.280 --> 16:14.490
but see how they're smiling?

16:15.200 --> 16:18.580
A couple that can get through
something like this while smiling

16:18.580 --> 16:21.270
is probably going to be okay,
no matter what happens.

16:22.260 --> 16:25.750
Meanwhile, here I am,
not even at the starting line.

16:25.980 --> 16:28.920
No! I can't give up yet!

16:28.920 --> 16:30.760
I need to try to reach Yanagi-sensei!

16:30.760 --> 16:34.210
S-Since it's almost time for lunch,

16:34.210 --> 16:36.140
why don't we head into
one of the restaurants?

16:38.600 --> 16:40.620
Sure, I'd love to!

16:43.140 --> 16:44.990
What are we getting on next?

16:45.880 --> 16:48.020
Why don't we grab lunch first?

16:48.020 --> 16:52.190
Good point. Hunger can be a
detriment to fun, after all.

16:52.190 --> 16:52.940
Yep.

16:58.960 --> 17:03.280
The sweets hunt and jungle
picnic were both great!

17:03.280 --> 17:06.380
Aren't theme parks just
the best, Chitose-chan?

17:06.380 --> 17:07.220
Yeah!

17:08.670 --> 17:10.170
Oh, I forgot!

17:10.540 --> 17:15.790
It looks like they were flirting just fine,
even if we weren't around to see it all.

17:17.070 --> 17:18.340
After them!

17:18.930 --> 17:21.180
Hang on, Chitose-chan!

17:21.460 --> 17:25.410
Oh, wow, a buffet!

17:25.410 --> 17:26.940
Grab anything you'd like.

17:28.640 --> 17:32.150
Since we're here, how about a game, darling?

17:32.150 --> 17:32.960
A game?

17:32.960 --> 17:35.790
Yeah. Instead of picking out your own food,

17:35.790 --> 17:40.200
we pick out the food we think the
other will like, and then exchange.

17:40.660 --> 17:42.840
I get it! That does sound like fun.

17:42.840 --> 17:46.730
I know exactly what foods you like, after all.

17:46.730 --> 17:48.460
I'm not gonna lose, though!

17:48.780 --> 17:50.170
Even at the buffet...

17:50.170 --> 17:53.810
There's a whole spectrum
of flirting out there, huh?

17:53.810 --> 17:57.900
That does seem like fun, though.
Let's go in and try it ourselves!

17:57.900 --> 17:59.260
I'm in!

17:59.260 --> 18:01.530
They're bound to notice us if we do!

18:01.530 --> 18:03.720
And then they'll get super mad!

18:05.730 --> 18:08.250
Not a problem! Now we've
got the perfect disguises.

18:08.250 --> 18:10.010
Not at all suspicious, right?

18:10.010 --> 18:12.480
I don't think I've seen anything
more suspicious, you dummy!

18:12.480 --> 18:13.730
Aw, don't sweat it.

18:13.730 --> 18:16.160
Put this on, Chitose-chan!

18:16.160 --> 18:16.720
Hey!

18:16.720 --> 18:19.490
How am I supposed to eat in this thing?!

18:21.900 --> 18:25.540
What kind of fool gets curry at a buffet?

18:25.540 --> 18:27.580
Fried shrimp, huh?

18:28.150 --> 18:30.230
Okay, that is way too much sausage!

18:31.060 --> 18:34.250
Oh, no, he put the cakes
next to the curry...

18:37.510 --> 18:40.300
Oh, man, she's gonna be so mad.

18:40.300 --> 18:42.290
Definitely.

18:42.940 --> 18:45.520
Serves him right! Not that I can see.

18:46.100 --> 18:48.140
How'd it go, darling?

18:49.020 --> 18:50.950
What's wrong, darling?

18:51.520 --> 18:54.020
Um, well, I, er...

18:54.720 --> 18:57.120
I think I'm gonna take another look!

18:57.120 --> 19:01.200
It's okay. I won't get mad,
no matter what you picked.

19:01.200 --> 19:02.660
Y-Yeah, but...

19:03.050 --> 19:06.090
Even if the cakes are
brushing against the curry,

19:06.090 --> 19:09.410
and the plating is total chaos,
I'll still enjoy it.

19:09.940 --> 19:11.660
How did you know?!

19:11.660 --> 19:15.420
Like I said, I know exactly
what you're like, darling.

19:15.680 --> 19:19.180
I see! Yet another way of flirting, then!

19:19.180 --> 19:20.930
This is so educational!

19:20.930 --> 19:23.020
It is not!

19:29.680 --> 19:32.190
Hi! I'm Muffy!

19:32.190 --> 19:32.950
Yay! I love Muffy!

19:32.950 --> 19:34.940
You can hug him and get a picture of it?!
Yay! I love Muffy!

19:34.940 --> 19:36.190
Yeah, you sure can!

19:38.480 --> 19:41.960
I bet he wants to hug her instead.

19:41.960 --> 19:44.240
I bet he wants to do a lot more than that.

19:44.240 --> 19:47.450
Quit being pervs at the theme park!

19:48.400 --> 19:49.600
Muffy!

19:49.600 --> 19:52.210
Thanks for coming today! Ha-ha!

19:52.480 --> 19:55.690
Wow! You're even fluffier than I imagined!

19:55.690 --> 19:58.940
I'm the fluffiest fella in the world! Ha-ha!

19:59.920 --> 20:01.970
So cute!

20:02.730 --> 20:04.970
Let's take a picture to remember this! Ha-ha!

20:05.370 --> 20:07.820
Seeing Tsukasa-chan so excited...

20:07.820 --> 20:11.010
It's a side of her I don't
usually see. That's so cute.

20:11.010 --> 20:13.480
I'm glad we came here.

20:13.740 --> 20:17.140
I guess Tsukasa-san likes
stuff like that, too.

20:17.140 --> 20:18.730
It is cute, after all.

20:19.570 --> 20:22.020
Do you wanna take a picture
too, Chitose-chan?

20:24.460 --> 20:25.790
Y-Yeah.

20:27.250 --> 20:28.740
So fluffy!

20:29.660 --> 20:30.850
So cute!

20:31.680 --> 20:33.700
Must be rough being a tsundere.

20:33.700 --> 20:34.750
Right?

20:35.510 --> 20:37.330
The sky has completely cleared up.

20:37.330 --> 20:40.150
The parade and fireworks come next.

20:40.150 --> 20:42.200
Really? That sounds great!

20:43.800 --> 20:46.010
There's Yanagi-sensei and Taniguchi-sensei!

20:46.300 --> 20:48.510
The vibe seems different now.

20:48.850 --> 20:50.940
Who knows...

20:50.940 --> 20:52.960
Maybe the magic is working on them!

20:53.990 --> 20:57.150
Do you think Taniguchi-sensei
told her how he feels?

20:59.340 --> 21:01.770
Things should be going in
a positive direction.

21:01.770 --> 21:04.560
And after today's events,
I'm sure about something!

21:04.560 --> 21:05.910
I really like her!

21:06.480 --> 21:08.930
I don't want to let anyone
else have Yanagi-sensei!

21:08.930 --> 21:12.660
Which is why I need to tell her how
I feel, so we can start dating!

21:15.490 --> 21:19.040
Thanks for inviting me out
today, Taniguchi-sensei.

21:19.330 --> 21:20.910
Oh, r-right.

21:20.910 --> 21:24.920
I had a lot of fun with you!

21:25.950 --> 21:27.440
I love her!

21:34.670 --> 21:36.690
It's so beautiful.

21:39.750 --> 21:41.040
Yanagi-sensei...

21:41.610 --> 21:46.700
I had a great time today with you, too.

21:46.700 --> 21:48.700
Really?

21:48.700 --> 21:51.320
You wanna get married, then?

21:51.950 --> 21:54.700
What... did you just say?

21:54.990 --> 21:57.100
Well, I mean...

21:59.220 --> 22:01.540
Er, sorry! I know that was sudden!

22:01.540 --> 22:03.210
It's just, y'know...

22:03.630 --> 22:05.470
Um, well...

22:05.470 --> 22:08.500
I felt really comfortable today.

22:08.500 --> 22:13.810
Like being with you all the time
makes sense, or makes me feel at ease...

22:13.810 --> 22:16.490
So I was thinking, with someone like that...

22:16.490 --> 22:19.230
Life would be really nice.

22:29.490 --> 22:31.740
I feel the same way.

22:35.170 --> 22:37.800
I like you, Yanagi-sensei.

22:43.360 --> 22:45.130
Now that's magical.

22:51.260 --> 22:53.780
Things are looking good, huh?

22:53.780 --> 22:56.070
Really! They get along so well.

22:57.200 --> 22:58.520
We're going home.

22:58.520 --> 23:00.020
You don't want to say hi?

23:01.080 --> 23:03.280
We had our fun already.

23:03.280 --> 23:05.670
I don't see the need for anything else.

23:07.030 --> 23:10.600
I guess even a professional wet blanket
knows when to respect the mood.

23:10.600 --> 23:13.030
What did you just call me?!

23:25.600 --> 23:28.710
I think Japanese people need to
be more casual about kissing!

23:28.710 --> 23:30.970
Well, it's a pretty subjective issue...

23:30.970 --> 23:32.840
Good morning kisses! Goodbye kisses!

23:32.840 --> 23:34.350
Kisses for a job well done! And...

23:34.350 --> 23:38.560
"Sorry, I really want to finish this quest
today, so go to bed before me" kisses!

23:38.560 --> 23:39.980
Now that's a practical one!
